---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Network engineer — routing, switching, automation and everything in between."
	pubDate={new Date('August 07 2026')}
>
	<p>
		Hi — I'm a <strong>network engineer</strong>. I spend my days keeping packets
		flowing and my nights breaking (then fixing) things in the lab. This site is my
		public notebook: designs, configs, troubleshooting write-ups and automation
		experiments.
	</p>

	<h2>$ cat ./experience.md</h2>
	<p>
		I work across the full network stack — from campus access and wireless, through
		the WAN and SD-WAN edge, into the data-center fabric. Lately I've been focused on
		<strong>network automation</strong> and <strong>telemetry</strong>: replacing
		manual CLI work with Python and Ansible, and swapping SNMP polling for streaming
		gNMI where I can.
	</p>

	<h2>$ ls ./certifications/</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>CCNA / CCNP Enterprise — routing &amp; switching</li>
		<li>Working toward CCIE / JNCIP</li>
		<li>AWS Certified — Advanced Networking (in progress)</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>$ ./skills --verbose</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Routing:</strong> BGP, OSPF, IS-IS, MPLS L3VPN, Segment Routing</li>
		<li><strong>Switching:</strong> VXLAN/EVPN, STP, MLAG, QinQ, spine-leaf fabrics</li>
		<li><strong>Automation:</strong> Python, Ansible, Netmiko, NAPALM, Nornir, Jinja2</li>
		<li><strong>Security:</strong> IPsec, zone-based firewalls, 802.1X, ACLs</li>
		<li><strong>Tooling:</strong> Wireshark, Grafana, InfluxDB, Git, Terraform, Docker</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>$ echo $CONTACT</h2>
	<p>
		Want to talk networking, automation or a lab build? Reach me via the links in the
		header, or open an issue on my GitHub. New posts land in the
		<a href="/blog">blog</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
